      "magnitude": "Pooled termination A/E 0.389 (z ~ -22.1, expected terminations 1302) — actual cardiovascular recoveries run at ~39% of the assumed rate, i.e. ~61% below baseline",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_ip_termination.csv: Cardiovascular pooled A/E 0.389 vs Cancer 0.999, Injury/Accident 0.974, Mental Health 1.005, Musculoskeletal 1.017, Other 0.983 — the deviation is confined to one diagnosis",
        "Expected terminations of 1302 is not a small cell; z ~ -22 is far beyond Poisson sampling noise, so this is not dispersion",
        "IP onset experience is level (overall A/E 1.0023, yearly 0.978-1.029), so the adverse experience is in duration/recovery, not in claim onset; other diagnoses' recoveries sit within ~1 z of baseline"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Re-examine the IP recovery/termination assumption for cardiovascular claims: validate diagnosis coding and 'resolved' status in claim-level data across duration months, check for data/coding gaps or misclassified diagnoses, quantify the resulting adverse impact on claim durations and IP liabilities, and update pricing/valuation termination assumptions for cardiovascular claims if the slower recovery is genuine and persistent."
    }
  ]
}

